          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The Active Atlas day trek is moderate and can be tailored to your preferred pace. Most travelers with average physical fitness comfortably complete the 3 to 4-hour guided hike through the Imlil Valley and Armed village. If you prefer a gentle nature walk or a more challenging summit ascent, your private mountain guide customizes the trail elevation on the spot."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do we visit authentic Berber villages during the Atlas hike?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. You hike through terraced walnut orchards, apple groves, and centuries-old Amazigh (Berber) villages like Armed, Tamatert, and Imlil clinging to the High Atlas slopes. You will enjoy a freshly prepared 3-course traditional Berber lunch on a panoramic rooftop terrace hosted by a local family, overlooking Mount Toubkal (4,167m)."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What gear and footwear should I wear for the Atlas Mountains?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Sturdy walking sneakers or lightweight hiking boots with good traction are essential for uneven dirt and cobblestone trails. Dress in comfortable layers (breathable shirt, fleece jacket or windbreaker), as mountain temperatures can be 5°C to 10°C cooler than Marrakech. Sunglasses, sunscreen, and a small daypack are recommended."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is private transport from Marrakech included in the Atlas tour?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. Your private English-speaking chauffeur picks you up directly from your Marrakech riad or hotel at 08:30 AM in an air-conditioned 4x4 or executive Mercedes minivan, driving 90 minutes through Asni and the Moulay Brahim Gorge to Imlil, and returning you to your door by 05:30 PM."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is the Active Atlas tour available year-round?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. The Imlil Valley is accessible all 12 months. Spring (March to May) brings lush green terraces and blooming apple blossoms; summer (June to August) offers a cool escape from Marrakech's desert heat; autumn (September to November) features crisp golden walnut foliage; and winter (December to February) treats you to stunning snow-capped views of Mount Toubkal."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
];
---
<Layout lang="it" title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogImage={ogImage} bodyClass={bodyClass} extraStyles={extraStyles} schema={schema}>
  <style is:inline slot="head">

    :root {
      --bg-cream: #f2eee6;
      --card-bg: #ffffff;
      --border-subtle: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
      --border-strong: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22);
      --text-main: #000000;
      --text-muted: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.72);
      --red: #f10b18;
    }

    *, *::before, *::after {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html, body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      background: #f2eee6 !important;
      color: #000000 !important;
      overflow-x: hidden;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    }

    main.roam-tour-main {
      background: #f2eee6 !important;
      color: #000000 !important;
      padding: 120px 24px 80px !important;
    }

    .roam-tour-wrapper {
      max-width: 960px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .roam-tour-badge {
